# Naming

Shared **entity Ids** and **Content prefixes** are canonical in:

`docs/governance/naming-and-versioning.md`

This file keeps **C++ / UPROPERTY** conventions for Cursor. Do not invent a parallel Id scheme here.

## C++ (UE prefixes — required)

| Kind | Prefix | Example |
|------|--------|---------|
| Actor | `A` | `ACity`, `ASimCameraPawn` |
| UObject | `U` | `UCityObject`, `UCityManagerSubsystem` |
| Struct | `F` | `FCityDefinition` |
| Enum | `E` | `ESeaRegion` (when added) |
| Interface | `I` | `IInteractable` (when added) |

- Module/system prefix in the type name: `City*`, `Sim*`, `UI*` / `SimHud*`, `Fleet*`, `Storage*`, `Market*`, `Trade*`, `Company*`, `Character*`, `Facility*`, `NpcAi*`, `Ship*`; planned: `Condition*`.
- **No Family\*** — Family design removed; do not add `Family_*` Ids or modules.
- Files: `CityActor.h` may own class `ACity` (short public name OK if unique).
- Bools: `b` prefix (`bIsValid`). Out-params: `Out*`.
- UPROPERTY/UFUNCTION `Category`: `"System"` or `"System|Sub"` (e.g. `"City|Storage"`, `"Market"`).

## Entity Ids (`FName`) — cross-system uniqueness

- Prefer **system-prefixed** Ids so names never collide across systems (Fleet / Goods / Character / …).
- Form: `<System>_<Name>` in PascalCase after the underscore. Examples:
  - Fleet: `Fleet_<序号>` (runtime serial; player mark is `PlayerCommandedFleetId`, not Id)
  - Ship: `Ship_<序号>`
  - Company: `Company_Player`
  - Goods: `Goods_Grain`
  - Character: `Char_PlayerLeader`, `Char_Npc_Advisor`
  - Facility: `Fac_London_Market`
- Character Id collision: append numeric suffix (`Char_Foo_2`).
- Do **not** use bare generic tokens (`Player`, `Default`, `Main`) as Ids.
- **Legacy exception**: existing City / sea-region Ids stay bare (`London`, `EuropeNW`, …). Do not rename without a migration plan. New systems must use prefixed Ids; do not introduce new bare Ids that could collide with cities or other systems.

## Content assets

| Asset | Prefix | Path |
|-------|--------|------|
| Blueprint | `BP_` | `Content/Blueprint/<System>/` (e.g. `Sim/BP_StrategicMapWaterBody`, `GameMode/BP_SimGameMode`) |
| Widget Blueprint | `WBP_` | `Content/UI/` or `Content/Blueprint/UI/` (e.g. `WBP_SimHud`, `Content/UI/City/WBP_CityPanel`; C++ parent under `Source/.../UI/`) |
| DataTable | `DT_` | `Content/<System>/` |
| Static mesh | `SM_` | domain folder |
| Material | `M_` | `Content/Materials/` |
| Texture | `T_` | domain folder; UI temp skins `T_UI_*` under `Content/Temp/UI/` |
| Map | `Map_` | `Content/Maps/Map_<SeaRegion>` |

- Temporary imports only under `Content/Temp/` — never treat as shipping content.
- Do not rename established Ids (`CityId`, `SeaRegionId`, established goods ids) without a migration plan.
